          "guid": "mss3x574g8t3g9gq",
          "message": {
            "text": "Checks the MAJOR only (not the exact version) because the docs pin CDN URLs to a major (kerfjs@4) on purpose — that's the design decision, and this gate enforces it.\n\nThree options were on the table (see the ticket). Option 1 — a gate asserting the pinned version equals package.json's exact version — was rejected: the pinned version changes meaning at every release, so that gate would fail on every single release and force a manual URL edit each time (more friction than the size/api gates, which only change when the underlying value actually moves). Option 2 — auto-rewriting the URLs in the release script — was rejected as riskier surgery on the resumable release state machine, and it only fires at release (manual drift between releases goes uncaught).\n\nMajor-only pins (chosen) resolve to the latest of that major, so they stay correct across every minor/patch and only go stale at a major bump. This gate catches exactly that boundary — plus any hand-edit typo — on every npm run check, not just at release. An illustrative exact pin in the prose (kerfjs@4.1.0 in the \"for reproducibility\" note) still passes, because major 4 matches; it correctly starts failing only once the major moves.\n",
            "markdown": "Checks the MAJOR only (not the exact version) because the docs pin CDN URLs to a major (`kerfjs@4`) on purpose — that's the design decision, and this gate enforces it.\n\nThree options were on the table (see the ticket). Option 1 — a gate asserting the pinned version equals `package.json`'s *exact* version — was rejected: the pinned version changes meaning at **every** release, so that gate would fail on every single release and force a manual URL edit each time (more friction than the size/api gates, which only change when the underlying value actually moves). Option 2 — auto-rewriting the URLs in the release script — was rejected as riskier surgery on the resumable release state machine, and it only fires at release (manual drift between releases goes uncaught).\n\nMajor-only pins (chosen) resolve to the latest of that major, so they stay correct across every minor/patch and only go stale at a major bump. This gate catches exactly that boundary — plus any hand-edit typo — on every `npm run check`, not just at release. An illustrative exact pin in the prose (`kerfjs@4.1.0` in the \"for reproducibility\" note) still passes, because major 4 matches; it correctly starts failing only once the major moves.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
